      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/frederica_delaware",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Frederica sits on the Murderkill River, just six miles from Delaware Bay, a factor that shaped its early commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/frederica_delaware",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early Frederica shipped bacon, beef, corn, wheat flour, cedar shingles, cheese, butter, tar, pitch, and hardwood boards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederica%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1857 Delaware Railroad diverted river traffic, causing Frederica’s decline as a major shipping hub.",
